  <revision rev="5" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>f74a598838978dca91c586a01dcaf042</srcmd5>
    <version>1.4.0</version>
    <time>1795023151</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>- Keep old style vendor script around
- Fix up pkg-config files
- Restore build-id again

- Fix the build with zig 0.17:
  * vendor.tar.zst: unpack the 37 zig packages into p/&lt;hash&gt;/;
    zig 0.17 stores fetched packages as compressed p/&lt;hash&gt;.tar.gz,
    which zig build --system cannot find, so the build stopped with
    &quot;package not found&quot; for uucode and translate_c
  * vendor.tar.zst: remove the prebuilt Windows, macOS and Java
    binaries and test fixtures that gettext, imgui, breakpad and
    sentry carry
  * vendor.sh: unpack the fetched packages, delete those binaries,
    and keep the test directories, which the translate_c build
    reads
  * Install with a relative lib dir, as zig 0.17 does not apply
    DESTDIR to an absolute one
  * Recreate the ghostty terminfo alias, a symlink that zig 0.17
    does not install
  * Fix prefix and libdir in libghostty-vt.pc and do not ship the
    static library
- The vendored libxml2 is not built, as fontconfig is linked from
  the system, so the package is not affected by:
  * CVE-2025-6021 (boo#1244594)
  * CVE-2025-8732 (boo#1247855)
- Spec cleanup

- Update to 1.4.0
  https://ghostty.org/docs/install/release-notes/1-4-0</comment>
    <requestid>1398422</requestid>
  </revision>
</revisionlist>
